window.GAKS_SEARCH = [{"t":"ADR-taf-v1-001-01 — tafbase stands alone","i":"ADR-taf-v1-001-01-tafbase-stands-alone","h":"doc/decisions/ADR-taf-v1-001-01-tafbase-stands-alone.html","s":"accepted","x":"ADR-taf-v1-001-01 — tafbase stands alone Decided: 2026-10-14 · George Petrov + Devin Decisions 1. tafbase is its own repository and its own corpus. It does not live inside IKC3. gaks.project.json declares it; the static GAKS bundle of PLAN-ikc-v3-079-01 delivers the corpus tools. This is the first real consumer of the foreign-project path. 2. The DSL is JSON, not EDN. The SUT model must be readable and writable from Java and Python with no Clojure dependency — the same reason gaks.project.json replaced the EDN declaration in IKC3. 3. Generate, don't interpret. Emitters write committed, reviewable test files (testlogin.py, LoginJourneyTest.java). A generic runtime interpreter was considered and refused: generated code diffs in a PR are legible; hidden magic is not. 4. Tracker integrations are declared adapters, not a hard dependency. tafbase core runs with no IKC3. The IKC3 adapter (fault reports, repaired-on-merge) is the first sink and the demo loop; JIRA and GitHub Issues adapters are additions of the same kind. 5. The IKC3 tracker is the first SUT, not a component of tafbase. Dogfooding means tests exercise the real platform and file reports into it — not that tafbase embeds it. 6. MIT license. The goals are exposure and adoption; copyleft and dual-licensing are refused. Consequences Doc ids take the taf subproject prefix (PLAN-taf-v1-NNN-NN); numbering is this repository's own. The IKC3 deployment tracker can file tickets for tafbase work only if this corpus is registered as a vault of the deployment — an open question, deferred to the first lane."},{"t":"PLAN-taf-v1-001-01 — tafbase: a DSL First test automation framework","i":"PLAN-taf-v1-001-01-tafbase","h":"doc/plans/PLAN-taf-v1-001-01-tafbase.html","s":"draft","x":"PLAN-taf-v1-001-01 — tafbase: a DSL First test automation framework Status: in progress tafbase declares a system under test (SUT) once, as data, and generates real test suites from the declaration. Python+Playwright is the first emitter; Java is the second, and the second exists to make the parity claim true. Generated suites report into pluggable tracker adapters; the first adapter is IKC3's fault reports, so a red test files a bug into the very platform the tests exercise. Release note (draft) New: a SUT declared once in JSON runs as a Python+Playwright suite; the same declaration refuses the same broken model the same way. Accepted by: T-taf-001 (parity of refusal, env -i, python3 only) New: a failed generated test files a fault report into a configured tracker through a declared adapter; the IKC3 adapter is the first. Accepted by: T-taf-002 Internal: the Java+Playwright emitter proves the same declaration generates equivalent suites in two languages. Accepted by: T-taf-003 (Python and Java emitters agree on the suite) What this does not do v1 generates static journeys only. Model-based generation — walks of the SUT graph, coverage-directed paths, journal replay — is declared in ADR-taf-v1-002-01 and arrives by lanes, not all at once. Lanes ▶ Lane TAF/PLAN-taf-v1-001-01/A-1 — the SUT model is JSON A SUT declares states, transitions and journeys in one JSON document. The loader validates shape, refusals name the broken clause, and no ambiguous form is guessed — one form only. Release note (draft) New: sut.model.json declares pages, actions and journeys; a broken model names its fault. Accepted by: T-taf-001 ▶ Lane TAF/PLAN-taf-v1-001-01/B-2 — the Python+Playwright emitter From a valid model, taf emit --lang python writes a runnable Playwright+pytest suite: page objects, journey tests, and a manifest mapping each test back to the model element that produced it. Release note (draft) New: one declaration produces a committed, reviewable pytest suite. Accepted by: T-taf-004 ▶ Lane TAF/PLAN-taf-v1-001-01/C-3 — tracker adapters and fault reports A test outcome flows to a declared sink. The IKC3 adapter files a fault report and links it to the test's model element; adapters are a declared kind so JIRA or GitHub Issues are additions, not rewrites. Release note (draft) New: a red test files a fault report into IKC3, named for its model element; the report repairs when the fix lands. Accepted by: T-taf-002 ▶ Lane TAF/PLAN-taf-v1-001-01/D-4 — the Java emitter proves parity --lang java emits the equivalent Playwright-Java + JUnit suite. Parity means: same model, same refusal text, same test names, same journey steps — the discipline measured in PLAN-ikc-v3-079-01 applied to a second axis. Release note (draft) New: the same declaration generates the Java suite; both emitters agree or both refuse. Accepted by: T-taf-003 ▶ Lane TAF/PLAN-taf-v1-001-01/E-5 — the tracker is the first SUT IKC3's tracker is the demo SUT: real UI (reader/tot islands), real API (th"}];
